<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Agbor</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 CE – 1897 CE (approx.) · capital Agbor</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ika kingdom west of the lower Niger, ruled by the Dein of Agbor and long within the sphere of the Benin Empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Agbor lies in the forest between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-city">Benin City</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>, among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ika-people">Ika</a>, an Igboid-speaking people with strong ties to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-people">Edo</a>. Its kingship is believed to date from around the 15th century, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> influence spread east toward the river, and its traditions combine Edo and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igbo-people">Igbo</a> elements.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Dein of Agbor ruled with title-holding chiefs and age-grade associations over yam-farming villages. Agbor paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oba-dynasty">Oba</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a> and adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> titles and regalia, while keeping its own dynasty and local religious practices.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the British conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> in 1897, Agbor came under British control and was incorporated into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/protectorate-of-southern-nigeria">Southern Nigeria</a>. The Dein of Agbor remains the traditional ruler of Agbor in Delta State.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1450 CE – 1897 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:88.56%;width:8.90%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 CE – 1897 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Agbor</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ika traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ika</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/nigeria">Nigeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Agbor, Ika kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1674&amp;focus=kingdom-of-agbor" aria-label="Kingdom of Agbor on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4852 1944 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Agbor lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5172 2200L5155 2197"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5155 2197h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5172 2200h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5172 2200h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Agbor. <a href="/atlas?year=1674&amp;focus=kingdom-of-agbor">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

